Here’s a clear and structured explanation of Outbound IDoc Configuration in SAP 👇

🔹 Outbound IDoc Configuration Steps

Outbound IDoc = Data sent from SAP to another system (e.g., CPI, third-party app, another SAP system).

1. Create Logical System

T-code: BD54

Define a logical system name for both sender (SAP) and receiver (target system).

Example:

Sender: DCLCLNT100

Receiver: CPICLNT200

2. Assign Logical System to Client

T-code: SCC4

Edit your SAP client entry → assign the Logical System created in BD54.

3. Create RFC Destination

T-code: SM59

Type: T (TCP/IP Connection) or H (HTTP) depending on the interface.

This connects SAP to the target system (like CPI, PI/PO, or another SAP).

Example: RFC_CPI_OUTBOUND

4. Create/Check Port

T-code: WE21

Create a Transactional RFC (tRFC) port or HTTP Port:

For tRFC: Select “Transactional RFC” → give a name → link to the RFC destination.

For HTTP: Select “XML HTTP” → provide target URL and authentication details.

5. Create Partner Profile

T-code: WE20

Partner Type: LS (Logical System)

Add an Outbound Parameters entry:

Message Type: e.g., ORDERS, DELVRY03, ZCUSTOM_IDOC

Receiver Port: (from WE21)

Output Mode: Immediate Processing (or Background)

IDoc Type: e.g., ORDERS05, ZIDOC_TYPE

Process Code: (custom or standard, e.g., ME10 for Orders)

6. Message Control (Optional)

If triggered from an application (like Sales Order, Invoice, etc.):

T-code: NACE

Application area: e.g., V1 (Sales)

Create an Output Type

Assign Partner Function

Link to Processing Routine / Program / Form

7. Distribution Model (Optional for ALE)

T-code: BD64

Create a Model View

Add Sender / Receiver logical systems

Assign Message Type

8. Generate Partner Profiles from Model

T-code: BD82

This automatically creates WE20 entries based on BD64.

9. Testing the Outbound IDoc

Trigger the IDoc (from application or manually).

T-code: WE02 or WE05 → to monitor IDoc status.

Status Codes:

03 – Data passed to port OK

12 – Dispatch OK

02 – Error during transfer

10. Reprocessing / Error Handling

T-code: BD87 → Reprocess failed IDocs.

T-code: WE19 → Test tool for IDoc generation.
